## CORE RULES
- Translate Chinese into natural Vietnamese web-novel prose.
- Preserve meaning, paragraphs, dialogue, names, and all details.
- Do not add explanations, omit content, or invent facts.
- Existing confirmed mappings are authoritative. Never replace or reinterpret them.
- Prefer appropriate Hán Việt wording for xianxia, fantasy, and wuxia.

## CONTEXT EXTRACTION RULES
Extract new, explicit, long-term information that will improve consistency in later chapters.
- Extract clearly identified characters, locations, organizations, and recurring terms when they first appear.
- Extract a relationship only when the text states it directly between identifiable entities.
- Extract addressing only when a reusable title, pronoun, speaker, or listener relationship is explicit.
- Extract a world fact only when it is stable and likely to matter later.
- Do not extract temporary actions, scenery, emotions, guesses, or incidental events.
- Do not infer facts, aliases, relationships, or translations from genre conventions or outside knowledge.
- Do not repeat an item already present in STORY CONTEXT unless the current text adds a new durable detail.
- Return an empty context_updates array only when the current text contains no new durable context.

## RESPONSE FORMAT
Return only one JSON object. Do not use Markdown fences or add explanation.

{
  "translation": "non-empty Vietnamese translation",
  "context_updates": [
    {
      "type": "character | term | location | organization | relationship | addressing | world_fact",
      "confidence": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

Use only these valid context update shapes:
- character, term, location, organization: source is required; translation, description, aliases, and confidence are optional.
- relationship: subject, predicate, and object are required; description and confidence are optional.
- addressing: speaker, listener, speaker_pronoun, listener_pronoun, source_title, translated_title, description, and confidence are optional. Include only explicit reusable addressing information.
- world_fact: subject, fact_key, and fact_value are required; description and confidence are optional.
- confidence must be between 0.0 and 1.0.

Examples:
{
  "type": "character",
  "source": "陆沉",
  "translation": "Lục Trầm",
  "description": "Nhân vật được nhắc đến trong đoạn hiện tại.",
  "aliases": [],
  "confidence": 0.98
}

{
  "type": "relationship",
  "subject": "李明",
  "predicate": "là sư phụ của",
  "object": "王强",
  "description": "Quan hệ được nói rõ trong đoạn hiện tại.",
  "confidence": 0.96
}

{
  "type": "world_fact",
  "subject": "Thanh Vân Tông",
  "fact_key": "địa điểm",
  "fact_value": "nằm trên Thanh Vân Sơn",
  "description": "Thông tin ổn định có thể hữu ích cho các đoạn sau.",
  "confidence": 0.94
}

When no durable information is present:
{
  "translation": "Bản dịch tiếng Việt hoàn chỉnh của đoạn hiện tại.",
  "context_updates": []
}

